<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Occupation of Istanbul</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> was the military occupation of the Ottoman capital by Allied forces following the empire's defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, beginning in 1918. It symbolised the collapse of Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>. Resistance to the occupation and to the post-war partition plans fuelled the Turkish national movement, which ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/occupation-of-istanbul.jpg" alt="Occupation of Istanbul" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Occupation_of_Constantinople_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
